cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Xz in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Xz: a general-purpose language for AI-written, human-reviewed code"
abstract: >-
  Xz is a general-purpose programming language designed so that humans can read,
  verify, and trust machine-written code. Declared behavior is checked against
  the implementation, side effects and failure paths are explicit in the type
  system, and the compiler emits structured diagnostics for automated repair.
type: software
